{"code":"var __defProp=Object.defineProperty;var __name=(target,value)=>__defProp(target,\"name\",{value,configurable:true});import{isDemonstrationProof,isDialectPrefixed,parseAcceptanceBlock,parseWhitelistedProof}from\"./review.js\";const GREP_PROOF_DIALECT_RULES=[\"  A `grep:` with no ` in <path>` clause is REFUSED, and the path may not contain `*` or `..`. The\",\"  pattern is a BASIC regex \\u2014 `[ * ^ $` are refused; `(` and `)` are safe, so `someSymbol(` is the\",\"  idiomatic way to prove a call site.\",\"  A `grep:` that must MISS after your change reads executed_fail and fails the very PR that\",\"  satisfies it \\u2014 restate it positively: grep the text your change ADDS, never what it removes.\",\"  A `grep:` PATTERN must never contain ` in ` \\u2014 the parser splits on the LAST ` in ` before a\",\"  path-like token, so a pattern carrying those words mis-splits into a different pattern and path.\"];const ACCEPTANCE_PROOF_GRAMMAR=[\"  ACCEPTANCE PROOFS are EXECUTED by the reviewer, and CI's `rmd lint-plan` REFUSES free prose on\",\"  any task you touch \\u2014 an unparseable proof means your own proposal cannot merge. Two forms only:\",'    proof: \"unit test: test/<name>.test.ts\"   \\u2014 runs that whole test file','    proof: \"grep: <pattern> in <path>\"        \\u2014 greps <pattern> in ONE real file or directory',\"  DEFAULT TO THE WHOLE-FILE `unit test:` FORM. You are FILING work, so its test does not exist\",\"  yet: the path form parses NOW and executes that file once someone implements it, while a test\",\"  title you invent would match zero tests forever. The path need not exist yet.\",...GREP_PROOF_DIALECT_RULES];const PR_BODY_ACCEPTANCE_GRAMMAR=[\"  ACCEPTANCE PROOFS are EXECUTED by the reviewer. A proof with no dialect is prose, and prose caps\",\"  the verdict, so the PR cannot merge without an operator. Under the `Acceptance:` header write\",\"  `- <claim> | <proof>` bullets, CONTIGUOUS, ONE PER PHYSICAL LINE \\u2014 never wrap a claim